---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LEGAL, SITE_NAME, TOOLS } from '../site';
const L = LEGAL;
const count = TOOLS.filter((t) => t.ready).length;
---

<LegalPage
  title="About & Contact"
  heading={`About ${SITE_NAME}`}
  showUpdated={false}
  description={`${SITE_NAME} is a free, private PDF toolkit that runs in your browser, operated by ${LEGAL.entity}. Learn how it works and how to contact us.`}
  summary={`${SITE_NAME} is a free set of ${count} PDF tools that run entirely in your web browser. Your files are processed on your own device and are never uploaded.`}
>
  <h2 id="why">Why we built it</h2>
  <p>
    Most online PDF tools ask you to upload your documents to their servers: contracts, payslips,
    medical letters, IDs. We think that's the wrong trade for a simple task like merging two files.
    Modern browsers are powerful enough to do the work themselves, so {SITE_NAME} does everything on
    your device. Nothing to upload, nothing to wait for, nothing left behind on someone else's server.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how">How it stays free</h2>
  <p>
    There are no accounts, subscriptions or paywalls. {SITE_NAME} is supported by advertising,
    which never has access to your files. Because the processing happens on your computer, our
    running costs stay low enough to keep every tool free and unlimited.
  </p>

  <h2 id="principles">Our principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your files stay yours.</strong> Processed locally, never uploaded, never stored.</li>
    <li><strong>No sign-up, no limits.</strong> Open a tool and use it.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest tools.</strong> Each tool page explains what it does and what it doesn't.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="company">Who runs {SITE_NAME}</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is owned and operated by {L.entity}, {L.entityType}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    For support, feedback, privacy or legal requests, email us. We read every message and reply as
    soon as we can.
  </p>
  <address>
    {L.entity}<br />
    {L.address.map((line) => (<>{line}<br /></>))}
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${L.email}`}>{L.email}</a>
  </address>
  <p class="muted">
    Please don't email us documents. We never need your files to help, and keeping them off email
    is the whole point.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
